wined3d: Present vsynced Vulkan swapchains in mailbox mode when available.

With FIFO, an application that renders faster than the display fills the
frame latency queue (three frames by default) and the swapchain, and then
shows each frame two or three refreshes after it was drawn. Affinity's
canvas does that once its buffers are fast (0050): the brush tip trailed
the cursor by about 90 ms instead of 50, flipping between the two from one
session to the next as the queue stayed filled or drained.

Mailbox never tears either, but shows the newest frame at each refresh and
does not block, so nothing queues up. Use it for swap intervals other
than 0 when the surface supports it, with at least three images. A present
then no longer throttles the application to the refresh rate; set
MailboxPresent (DWORD) to 0 under HKCU\Software\Wine\Direct3D to restore
FIFO.

Measured with 0050 on an Arc A750 under a nested KWin (Xwayland offers
IMMEDIATE, MAILBOX, FIFO and FIFO_RELAXED): the canvas present queue went
from 37-51 ms to under 1 ms, and present to completion from 16 ms to 8 ms.

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c b/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
index 258692f..41fd48d 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1041,6 +1041,20 @@ static HRESULT wined3d_swapchain_vk_create_vulkan_swapchain(struct wined3d_swapc
     }
 
     vk_present_mode = VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR;
+    /* With FIFO, an application that renders faster than the display fills
+     * the frame latency queue and then shows every frame two or three
+     * refreshes late; Affinity's brush trailed the cursor by about twice as
+     * much. Mailbox still never tears, but shows the newest frame at each
+     * refresh and does not block, so nothing queues up. It also means a
+     * present no longer throttles the application to the refresh rate;
+     * MailboxPresent=0 in the Direct3D key restores FIFO. */
+    if (swapchain_vk->s.swap_interval && wined3d_settings.mailbox_present
+            && wined3d_swapchain_vk_present_mode_supported(swapchain_vk, VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR))
+    {
+        vk_present_mode = VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR;
+        if (image_count < 3 && (!surface_caps.maxImageCount || surface_caps.maxImageCount >= 3))
+            image_count = 3;
+    }
     if (!swapchain_vk->s.swap_interval)
     {
         if (wined3d_swapchain_vk_present_mode_supported(swapchain_vk, VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR))
diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c b/dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c
index ec34aa3..29d2e61 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ struct wined3d_settings wined3d_settings =
     .pci_device_id = PCI_DEVICE_NONE,
     .multisample_textures = TRUE,
     .sample_count = ~0u,
+    .mailbox_present = TRUE,
     .max_sm_vs = UINT_MAX,
     .max_sm_ps = UINT_MAX,
     .max_sm_ds = UINT_MAX,
@@ -444,6 +445,8 @@ static BOOL wined3d_dll_init(HINSTANCE hInstDLL)
         }
         if (!get_config_key_dword(hkey, appkey, env, "strict_shader_math", &wined3d_settings.strict_shader_math))
             ERR_(winediag)("Setting strict shader math to %#x.\n", wined3d_settings.strict_shader_math);
+        if (!get_config_key_dword(hkey, appkey, env, "MailboxPresent", &wined3d_settings.mailbox_present))
+            TRACE("Mailbox presentation %s.\n", wined3d_settings.mailbox_present ? "enabled" : "disabled");
         if (!get_config_key_dword(hkey, appkey, env, "MaxShaderModelVS", &wined3d_settings.max_sm_vs))
             TRACE("Limiting VS shader model to %u.\n", wined3d_settings.max_sm_vs);
         if (!get_config_key_dword(hkey, appkey, env, "MaxShaderModelHS", &wined3d_settings.max_sm_hs))
